MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m01_01: Hi there! What pretty plumage you've got!
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m01_02: Hi! It's nice to see you again! How are you?
MID_SV_Bird_Kai1_m01_01: You have really pretty feathers!
MID_SV_Bird_Kai1_m01_02: It's good to see you again.
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m01_01: You will not flee?
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m01_02: Heh. You are strange.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m01_01: Do you not fear humans?
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m01_02: What an odd bird you are.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m01_01: You're downright beautiful.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m01_02: Well, aren't you a charmer?
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m01_01: You have stunning feathers.
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m01_02: Good to see you again. You're looking well.
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m01_01: Well, you're a pretty little thing, aren't you?
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m01_02: Haha! Glad you're doing well, friend.
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m01_01: Oh my! How adorable.
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m01_02: I'm glad to see you're doing well!
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m01_01: What a very curious-looking bird.
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m01_02: I'm glad to see you again.
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m01_01: Where did you come from, little bird?
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m01_02: I'm glad to see you're doing well!
MID_SV_Bird_Tia1_m01_01: Hehe. You're very well-behaved, aren't you?
MID_SV_Bird_Tia1_m01_02: Hello again. How have you been?
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m01_01: Hey there. Where'd you come from?
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m01_02: Hey, how are you doing?
MID_SV_Bird_Pet1_m01_01: Hello. I'm glad I could meet you.
MID_SV_Bird_Pet1_m01_02: Happy to know you're still doing well!
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m01_01: What a cute little bird.
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m01_02: Heh, so we meet again!
MID_SV_Bird_Max_m01_01: Hi! Nice to meet you.
MID_SV_Bird_Max_m01_02: Good seeing you again.
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m01_01: Mwahaha! Found my prey!
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m01_02: This is your unlucky day.
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m01_01: You're not scared of me?
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m01_02: Heh heh. You're a cute little fella.
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m01_01: What a lovely bird.
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m01_02: Haha! We meet again.
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m01_01: What a fascinating fowl.
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m01_02: You captivate me!
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m01_01: You are rather well-behaved.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m01_02: A delightful reunion, is it not?
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m01_01: Agh! You're so cute!
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m01_02: The breeze let me know that you'd come.
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m01_01: What a friendly bird you are!
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m01_02: You look like you're doing well. I'm glad.
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m01_01: Huh... You're quite the mystery, aren't you?
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m01_02: Still as puzzling as ever...
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m01_01: Don't see birds like you every day.
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m01_02: Hey, you're actually kinda cute.
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m01_01: Where did you come from, little one?
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m01_02: You get cuter every time I see you!
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m01_01: What a gorgeous creature...
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m01_02: You look well. I'm glad...
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m01_01: You're...not like normal birds.
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m01_02: Back again? You're an odd one.
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m01_01: What a strange bird. Where did you come from?
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m01_02: You're back again! Glad to see you're OK!
MID_SV_Bird_Lor1_m01_01: Looks like you're not scared of people.
MID_SV_Bird_Lor1_m01_02: Nice to see you. How's it going?
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m01_01: What beauty you bring...
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m01_02: You're as graceful as ever. How wonderful.
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m01_01: What an elegant presence...
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m01_02: I'm glad to encounter you again.
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m01_01: You seem to be quite well-acclimated to people.
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m01_02: Heh, how adorable.
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m01_01: Friendly bird, aren'tcha?
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m01_02: You're pretty cute for a birdie!
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m01_01: Wow, you're pretty bold for a bird.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m01_02: Where did you come from?
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m01_01: What a magnificent bird.
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m01_02: I hope this won't be our last meeting.
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m01_01: So elegant. Where did you come from?
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m01_02: I'd have expected you to fear the Demon Bear.
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m01_01: Ah, did the wind lure you here?
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m01_02: What a fine day this is.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m01_01: Hey, bird! You wanna chat?
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m01_02: Where do you keep turning up from?
MID_SV_Bird_Moo1_m01_01: You're really well-behaved.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo1_m01_02: We meet again! I'm glad you're well!
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m01_01: Were you lured by my flowery fragrance?
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m01_02: Oh, it's you! Heehee! How do you do?
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m01_01: Well, you're looking very calm. How are you doing?
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m01_02: Hey there! You're looking good!
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m01_01: Yes, let's both rest our wings a bit.
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m01_02: You came back! Shall we chat?
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m01_01: Uh, there's some kinda weird bird here.
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m01_02: Huh, you decided you like me or something?
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m01_01: Do you have a name, maybe?
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m01_02: You came back! I haven't seen you in a while!
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m01_01: What a strange bird. You look like something right\nout of one of my epic tales.
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m01_02: Hey there. Up for hearing some of my epic tales?
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m01_01: A curious bird... Our meeting must be fate.
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m01_02: We meet again? Indeed, fate is at play.
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m01_01: What a gentle bird.
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m01_02: I always feel at ease, seeing you...
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m01_01: What nobility of feather! You are welcome in\nour presence.
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m01_02: Your aerial journeys here must be tiring!
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m01_01: Oh! How unexpected! I like a good diversion!
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m01_02: Alright, let's enjoy each other's company!
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m01_01: My, how cute!
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m01_02: Oh goodness! We meet again.
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m01_01: You seem...different from other birds.
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m01_02: Here we are again. A stellar meeting!
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m01_01: You're not going to fly away? How gentle you are.
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m01_02: You seem well as ever. What a relief.
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m01_01: This bird would fetch a nice price!
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m01_02: Fancy as ever, bird.
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m01_01: Hey, you gettin' enough to eat?
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m01_02: There you are. Been hopin' to see you!
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m01_01: Oooh! Who's a good wittle birdie?
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m01_02: Aww, who's a good birdie? Ha ha!
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m01_01: How very cute...
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m01_02: Ach! You li'l flapper. I love seein' ya.
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m01_01: Used to being around people, huh? What a\nwell-behaved bird you are!
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m01_02: You again? What a strange bird you are.
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m01_01: Why, hello! What a gallant bird you are.
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m01_02: I'm glad to see you again!
MID_SV_Bird_Cle_m01_01: 
MID_SV_Bird_Cle_m01_02: 
MID_SV_Bird_Mys_m01_01: 
MID_SV_Bird_Mys_m01_02: 
MID_SV_Bird_Nat_m01_01: For a bird, you have quite a presence.
MID_SV_Bird_Nat_m01_02: Hello again. Stay a moment?
MID_SV_Bird_Hri_m01_01: Let's kill some time together, little bird.
MID_SV_Bird_Hri_m01_02: Glad you came. I need a distraction.
MID_SV_Bird_Tro_m01_01: Mind keeping me company?
MID_SV_Bird_Tro_m01_02: You must be tired. Take a moment to rest\nyour wings.
MID_SV_Bird_Cen_m01_01: You look quite elegant for one who lives in the wild.
MID_SV_Bird_Cen_m01_02: You seem well. This pleases me greatly.
MID_SV_Bird_Asw_m01_01: Care to join me? Hmm?
MID_SV_Bird_Asw_m01_02: We meet again. Spreading our wings together.
MID_SV_Bird_Kou_m01_01: You carry yourself strangely for a bird.
MID_SV_Bird_Kou_m01_02: You came. I've been waiting.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m01_01: It is nice to find fellowship with animals.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m01_02: Let us confer, as two spirits most at home in\nthe wild.
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m01_01: Resting your wings? So's the Rukh...
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m01_02: Welcome back, buddy!
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_01: Do you think I'll ever be better with a spear than\nmy dad?
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_02: I can't stand cowardice. But I guess maybe that's\nbetter than getting used to it.
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_03: Sometimes, it's like people can guess what's on my\nmind. Am I that easy to read?
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_04: It's neat how quick birds can move. You look like you\ncould dodge any attack!
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_05: Today's a perfect day for fishing! You wanna come\nalong with me sometime?
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_06: I hear pretty birdsong sometimes. Is that you?
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_07: It's nice to unwind a little sometimes, huh?
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_08: How do you become an adult, anyway? It seems like\neveryone has to overcome a challenge to do it.
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_09: I wonder what the world looks like through\nyour eyes.
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m02_10: I bet it'd be fun to play hide-and-seek with you!
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_01: You do not mind if I touch you?
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_02: Still your mind. Let it be a secluded pond. Give\nyourself to silence. It is good to meditate.
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_03: I cannot find a fitting opponent for a duel. I am\nparched. Not my throat, but my soul.
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_04: A sea beast diverted me to this land. Perhaps it was\nthe hand of fate.
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_05: I sense in you something profound and menacing.\nPerhaps Answerer can expose it.
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_06: I like your eyes. They are as bright as sunlight.
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_07: I detest restraints. And you?
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_08: I have slain giant birds. Yet I feel I would enjoy\nbattling you even more.
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_09: You show no signs of fear. That is unusual. You\nare unusual.
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m02_10: I dislike those who fetter me... They constrain joy\nand supply boredom.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_01: We see ourselves as indebted to Yu Phas, so we\ncannot help but afford her the proper reverence.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_02: My retainer winces at the sight of the sketches I\nenjoy drawing. I blame this new arm of mine.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_03: In truth, I have no fondness for insects. Do you eat\nthem often?
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_04: As a child of Damascar, I cannot be expected to\nplace my trust in the temples.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_05: I yearn to be a queen that Yu Phas and the people of\nSaramis can take pride in.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_06: If I can make this world a place where my people\ncan thrive, I will consider myself satisfied.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_07: I find myself somewhat weary of late...
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_08: As a child, I used to fall asleep listening to bedtime\nstories and lullabies.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_09: There is a firm resolve in your eyes not often seen\nin birds.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m02_10: I have considered training my spear technique\nagainst you. Surely you can avoid my blows.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_01: Birds are good at singing, aren't they? So how about\nI play my vihuela and you sing for me?
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_02: In the middle of playing, I often find I'm returning\nto songs from back home. I guess I'm nostalgic.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_03: It's nice being showered in applause. If you want to\nexperience it, come fly to me when I'm performing.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_04: The key to dancing is good posture. Slouch, and\nyou'll only give a pitiful performance.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_05: I can't stand snakes. If there was a snake here,\nyou would chase it away, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_06: If you see me on a horse ride, you'd better swoop\ndown and say hello.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_07: I often wonder if there's any point in praying to\nthe gods.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_08: I'm willing to use any means—make any sacrifice—\nto achieve my goal. Is that wrong?
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_09: I've been having trouble sleeping. I wonder if hearing\na lullaby would help.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m02_10: The next time I make food, will you try it? Humans\ndon't seem to like my cooking, but maybe a bird...
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_01: I always feel sorry for wild animals put in cages.\nIs that strange?
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_02: Even a short jaunt can help improve one's mindset.\nDo you like exercise?
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_03: Humans deceive each other for their own gain. That\ndoesn't seem like something you'd ever do.
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_04: My grandmother was elderly when she taught me\nhow to wield a sword. I'm still in awe of her.
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_05: Clever bird. I wonder if I could teach you to play\nboard games.
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_06: Will the day ever come that I am at peace—that I\ncan bury my nose in a book and lose myself in it?
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_07: Do you enjoy flight? It sounds nice, flying above\nnations, looking down at people to see how they fare.
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_08: If I could fly like you, I'd be able to make my way\nanywhere so much more quickly.
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_09: I hear that I'm sung about by the bards. Am I a good\nsubject for songs?
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m02_10: Hope is what gives one the will to live. But I don't\nreally know—do birds feel hope?
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_01: Ever been out to the sea? Your hopes, your dreams—\nall the adventure you could ever want is out there.
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_02: If I'm being honest, I don't really like the sight of\nblood... It makes fighting kind of a pain.
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_03: Follow your heart, that's what I always say. Bird or\nnot, you should live that way too.
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_04: Nothing's more annoying than some drunk moron in\na bar, am I right? 
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_05: There are lands out there with cultures we've still yet\nto experience. It's exciting, isn't it?
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_06: One day, I'll do something that will make the whole\nworld see me. You believe me, don't you?
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_07: As exciting as things seem, I've been pretty bored\nlately. Flown anywhere interesting recently?
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_08: Ugh... Sorry, friend. Doing paperwork all day has got\nme in a mood.
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_09: Your eyes... I've never seen a bird with eyes\nlike yours.
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m02_10: I've fought plenty of monsters, but there was one that\nreally put me to the test. Care to hear the story?
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_01: I feel like I've known you for a long time.
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_02: I've been growing some pretty flowers that have\nbloomed recently. I'd love to show them to you.
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_03: Credna often gets his clothing dirty. I don't mind\ndoing laundry, but I find that troublesome.
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_04: I'd love to explore different places with you. Doesn't\nthat sound fun?
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_05: I heard someone singing on the street. I found it so\nlovely that I was very enchanted.
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_06: From time to time, I return souls back to the great\ncycle, so that they can find peace.
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_07: I struggle with intricate work like embroidery. \nDo you think I'll ever get better at such things?
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_08: I wish you were here when I sometimes look up at\nthe night sky. Is that too much to ask?
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_09: For some reason, when I look into your eyes, I find\nthat memories begin to surface...
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m02_10: The scent of the oil I use on my body makes animals\nwary. Doesn't it bother you?
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_01: I've been told a prince might help me to realize my\npotential. Does that make sense to you?
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_02: I tend to bombard others with questions when I'm\ncurious. Should I try to rein myself in a little bit?
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_03: I practice a martial art unique to Kunlun. Would you\nlike to see?
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_04: Oh! There is a cat over there! I'm sorry. I'm not good\nwith cats.
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_05: My fortune-telling says a difficult fate awaits you.\nI wonder if I made a mistake in my prediction?
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_06: If I could fly like you, I wonder if I'd be able to swoop\nin and save those I must protect.
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_07: I get so embarrassed when someone looks after me.\nMaybe that makes me childish?
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_08: Sometimes I upset people because there are so many\nthings I don't know.
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_09: Why is it that, when I look at you, I feel like\nI know you?
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m02_10: Have you noticed that, when you like someone, their\nvoice sounds so special to you?
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_01: Technique is important, yes. But without knowledge\nof why it works, it won't be of much use.
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_02: These glasses are pretty nice, don't you think?\nThey're a hand-me-down from my grandfather.
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_03: If something bad is going to happen no matter what,\nis there any point in fighting it?
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_04: You have such beautiful plumage. Do you mind if I\ntake a closer look?
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_05: I might be inexperienced, but I've studied hard and\nlearned more than most people!
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_06: I like to lie in the warm sun. Do you like it too?
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_07: I'd love to be a bird. I'd fly through the open windows\nand right into the temple library.
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_08: It's bad to overthink things, isn't it? It makes your\nhead go all fuzzy.
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_09: I'll always remember being with Grandpa when I\nwas little. We heard a bard sing the prettiest song.
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m02_10: I can see such intelligence in your eyes. I think we\ncould get along!
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_01: Taking it easy makes me sleepy... Hey, if I fall asleep,\nwill you wake me up?
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_02: Some animals make all kinds of racket. But you don't\ndo that, do you?
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_03: I had a dream about a beautiful bird... I wonder if it\nwas a friend of yours.
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_04: There's a ginji tree not far from here. We should\ngo together and pick some of the fruit!
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_05: Everyone's fighting. It's scary, but I'm doing my best!
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_06: I like clouds. They're so big, and it's neat to see all\nthe shapes they can take.
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_07: What should I do when I get so scared my legs start\nshaking and I can't move?
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_08: It's nice to walk around the forest and listen to\nall the sounds the animals make, huh?
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_09: I just don't know what to do about these feelings I\nhave for Tialla.
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m02_10: I look at you and... You make me feel like I can face\neven the most difficult things in life.
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_01: I feel like sometimes there's just no avoiding\nsnapping at your superiors.
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_02: I think this hairstyle is quite lovely. What do\nyou think?
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_03: I enjoy a good fish dinner, but you can't eat nothing\nbut fish every day, can you?
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_04: I can save money, yes, but I feel like the odds are low\nthat it'll start increasing on its own.
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_05: Do you think I'll have a happy family in the future?
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_06: What do you do when there's someone you like and\nyou want them to notice you?
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_07: I've been so exhausted lately. I could really do with\nsome pampering...
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_08: I could listen to bards sing all day. Their songs are\nso lovely.
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_09: I've noticed something interesting. I find just looking\nat you to be unusually soothing.
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m02_10: You're so cute! Can I take you home with me?
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_01: Ahh, I'm feeling great since I got to let my freak\nloose! How 'bout you?
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_02: Lookin' for a new look? How about a little birdie-\nblood dye job? Heh heh heh!
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_03: Made this costume myself. Pretty good uniform for\nthe Infernal Clown, don't ya think?
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_04: Guh, there's nothing I hate more than people who act\nhigh and mighty. I wanna yank out their guts!
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_05: Guuuh. Too many nasty stories. I'm gonna sleep—\nkeep an eye out.
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_06: I can't arouse suspicion. Will I look more like a clown\nif you're perched on my wrist?
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_07: Bertrand's so serious! The guy hardly ever takes\na joke. Y'know how hard that is for me?
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_08: Makeup's great. It hides your blood, your tears...\nyour crimes. You wanna get made up?
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_09: Birds, you're so lucky. In a flash, you can fly out to\nmurder scenes! Heh heh heh!
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m02_10: I'm tired—almost like I'm sick. I'm at such a low\npoint... I can't take it!
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_01: I never forget to train. If your body's in shape,\nthere's nothing you can't do!
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_02: No matter how hard he gets knocked down, my\nbrother keeps gettin' up. He's got spirit, that guy!
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_03: Hey, if some bully ever comes at you, you talk to me.\nI'll twist 'em in knots!
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_04: They say I got giant's blood. Bwahaha. It's funny!
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_05: The chief of my old tribe was a jerk. If you ever\nsee him, let me know, and I'll knock him out.
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_06: My head's spinning... When people talk about stuff\nthat's complicated, I get dizzy.
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_07: Ugh, busywork makes me so mad! Is there some way\nfor me to feel better?
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_08: People like having me around in battles, but other\nthan that, usually not.
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_09: When I think about how my brother got sent to the\narena—what he's been through—I get all teary eyed...
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m02_10: Don't sit on my hand. I'm worried I might squish you.
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_01: I trained as a warrior in the land of Sai. Would you\nconsider going there? You might like it.
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_02: I have a talent for estimating the number of soldiers\nthe enemy has. Useful, don't you think?
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_03: Your feathers have such a nice sheen to them.\nI wonder if they'd make for good writing tools.
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_04: I doze off after a little drink. Of course, I'd do it even\nmore easily if you sang for me too...
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_05: I'm proud of how well I've trained my body. Watch\nme in the colosseum and you'll see.
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_06: Ahaha... Do you think my behavior helps me blend in\nat the colosseum?
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_07: I like taking time to maintain my weapons. It's\nsoothing, and it has practical value, of course.
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_08: No matter their hardships, those with true power will\nsoar in time. Do you know what I mean by "soar"?
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_09: One has to be ruthless on the battlefield...but it's\nnever easy ending a young soldier's life.
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m02_10: There's a tea in the eastern lands said to only get\nbetter as it ages. Would you want to try it?
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_01: My last work was a masterpiece—but my next will\nbe even better. Yes! For I am always improving.
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_02: In moments of reflection, a demon taunts me, telling\nme I have no talent. Have you heard its voice too?
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_03: I will read you the masterpiece by my father Aeneus.\nIt's powerful enough to move even your avian heart!
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_04: Ahh, how I adore the city. You can sit back and\nwitness the bustle, the confusion—the ecstasy!
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_05: It's too bad you don't speak any human languages.\nI'm sure you'd have tales to tell.
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_06: I grew up in a home surrounded by natural beauty,\nwhere I awoke each morning to birdsong.
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_07: Intoxicants add color to one's experiences—bring out\na new side to any conversation! Don't you agree?
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_08: Had I wings like yours, I could fly at once to any\nresearch subject I wanted. Imagine it!
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_09: Through the temples, I've been given so many story\nideas! In that way the temples are a generous patron.
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m02_10: I'm partial to birds' faces—not like fishes', with those\nsoulless eyes. Mirrors reflecting nothing. Gah!
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_01: Simply catching sight of a thing of beauty is enough\nto lift the spirits.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_02: I have feigned the role of a missionary for years, yet\nthese simple beasts do not question it. Amazing.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_03: Is this land strange, or have I become strange? I find\nI cannot say.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_04: I am ill-suited to physical labor. Those who are\nshould be the ones to do it. Obvious, isn't it?
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_05: In this land, the sun's rays are relentless. I wish for\nsomething to block them.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_06: The plants of Dagda are of much interest to me.\nI would observe and sketch many more.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_07: What, then, is the purpose of celebrating the day of\none's birth? It escapes me.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_08: I have spent some time with this guise by now.\nI have, hmm, acclimated to it.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_09: You are the best kind of beast—no foolish words or\nwasted actions.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m02_10: How beautiful you are. A fine specimen for my\nscalpel, hmm?
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_01: What I hate most are liars. It's not good to deceive\npeople and then laugh about it to yourself.
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_02: If you're hungry, come find me! I'll slip you some\ntasty fish!
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_03: I hope my mom's doing OK. If I could fly like you, I'd\ngo see her.
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_04: My dad taught me everything I know about the sea.\nI wonder if I'm shaping up to be like him.
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_05: I hate being looked down on. But I guess a refined\nlady can't wallop her foes...can she?
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_06: Sometimes the guys in Dagsion turn my head, but...\nNo! Sweetie's the one for me!
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_07: My mom and dad always said I have pretty eyes.\nWhat do you think?
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_08: You know, you don't smell like other birds. Hold still.\nLet me check!
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_09: When I'm all by myself fishing, I like to sing. Just\nme, the waves, the wind, and my voice.
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m02_10: All the nobles like to throw flashy parties, or so I\nhear. What's so great about parties?
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_01: I'm not the best singer. I enjoy it, but I can't carry\na tune.
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_02: Say there's a guy in the tavern causing a fuss and I\nneed to punch him out. Should I avoid the face?
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_03: My sister taught me how to cook. She's incredible.\nOne taste and your heart just soars.
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_04: Just because a mom's marriage failed doesn't mean\nher daughter will make the same mistake. Right?
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_05: It's good to get strong. That way you're ready when\nit's time to kick out your good-for-nothing husband!
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_06: Be careful out there. If you see someone suspicious,\njust fly off, quick as you can!
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_07: I wonder how much strength is in that body. Maybe I\nshould just give you a little squeeze.
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_08: Money is the root of hardship. Not that you need to\nworry about that!
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_09: Do you have someone dear to you? I hope so. Do\nwhatever you can to protect them.
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m02_10: Owing debts is no good. As long as they're hanging\nover you, you can't think straight.
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_01: In my homeland, I lived a life of hiding... But in\nDagda, I'm free to be myself. Do you like it here?
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_02: Your feathers are simply gorgeous. Perhaps, one day,\nI can draw your portrait.
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_03: To be honest, sometimes I get so annoyed at my own\njealous feelings. I wish I could control them better...
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_04: I know I can't return home... But...sometimes I can't\nhelp but pine for what's gone...
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_05: Hey... If you ever see me become a beast, remember\nthat you mustn't approach me, alright?
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_06: You seem far sharper than the average bird. How\nwould you like to be a pet at the company?
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_07: Back then, when I was being hunted for my crest,\nI thought if I was a bird, maybe I could just fly away.
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_08: I can't stand a messy desk. If it's just a little bit out\nof sorts, I get an overwhelming urge to clean it.
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_09: Talimun has saved me in far more ways than one.\nAttending his misadventures is a small price to pay.
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m02_10: I can't read your thoughts like other animals...\nAre you really a bird?
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_01: Just because my ancestors were from Damascar\ndoesn't mean I pray to Yu Phas too.
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_02: In the field, nice guys always die fast. One minute,\nthey're cracking jokes, and the next...they're gone.
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_03: You know, I've always liked carving little wooden\nstatues. Maybe, one day, I'll carve you.
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_04: It's not too hard to be a merc, really. Fly over a\nbattlefield, and maybe you'll see some in action!
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_05: Launching a surprise attack is probably easier if you\ncan fly, huh? As long as no archers are around.
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_06: Now, if I could fly from battlefield to battlefield?\nMan, that would be the life.
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_07: Nosy people drive me up the wall. You know what\nI mean?
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_08: Sometimes, even when I'm not on the battlefield, I\nfeel this...tension in me, you know?
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_09: You're a strange one, aren't you? An animal that\ncares about living longer is usually more careful.
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m02_10: You're in the pink of health. Like you could\nsurvive anywhere.
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_01: One day, I'd love to be the main character of some\ngrand adventure. Would you want to come with me?
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_02: I saw this couple the other day, and they had so\nmuch passion! Kinda made me jealous...
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_03: Ugh! Gummy, sticky, greasy... I just hate dirty things.
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_04: Dante's work is amazing! Here, let me read you\nsomething!
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_05: I've been working so hard at the company. Whew!\nI think I need a vacation.
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_06: You know, I do a little bit of writing myself. I should\nwrite something with you as the main character.
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_07: Father always said I was a fantastic swordsman.\nCouldn't ever impress him with axes, though...
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_08: If I had wings? I'd travel the world and see\neverything this life has to offer.
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_09: Ugggh. Turns out, the person I like already has a\npartner... How will I ever recover...
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m02_10: You're pretty smart for a bird. Are you one of those\nspirits in disguise like in the stories?!
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_01: There are times when I can't take my mind off of the\none I adore... That's normal, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_02: Oh... I'm sorry... I suddenly feel like crying...
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_03: Sometimes when I read poetry, I swear it's almost\nlike I'm listening to music.
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_04: Love is a strange thing... Have you ever had feelings\nfor someone?
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_05: Maybe the reason I'm drawn to you is because, \nlike that person, you're hard to grasp...
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_06: If you're ever hurt, come find me, and I'll heal you.
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_07: Romance has always been a bit tough for me to\ngrasp. Maybe a friend like you is all I need.
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_08: Your eyes are so kind. They make me feel safe...
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_09: War and pain, fighting and hate... All of it just makes\nme sad... I'd like to avoid those things if I can.
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m02_10: Um... Doesn't being with me...bore you?
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_01: Poisonous plants will harm people, but they can be\nmade into medicine. As always, knowledge is key.
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_02: Orchel once saved my life. It's only natural that I\nwant to return the favor, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_03: I don't need to sleep on a bed. I can rest anywhere.\nIs it the same for you?
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_04: I know how to preserve meat by applying an herbal\nrub and smoking it. Do you like fragrant food?
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_05: You have a strangely penetrating gaze. Your eyes\nwould be an advantage in battle.
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_06: My tattoos mark me as a member of the Har Hali\nclan. I left them years ago, but they're still part of me.
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_07: I've been all over, doing work as a messenger for a\ntemple. But I've never seen a bird like you until now.
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_08: Do you worship Balor? I used to long ago, but I don't\nthese days.
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_09: I'm happy with my life now. There's no reason to\nworry about me.
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m02_10: You need agility to survive in forests. I wonder, are\nyou agile when you're in trees?
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_01: Even if it gets kinda boring, I can't complain if I've\ngot a place to sleep and enough to eat.
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_02: I'm pretty happy with my life now. But my heart goes\nout to my ol' street-orphan friends...
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_03: Birds eat fish, right? I'll catch a big one for you\nsometime!
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_04: You live in the forest, right? So tell me...how do you\nfeel about ghosts?
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_05: I don't know who my parents are, but I don't really\ncare. Things are good now. That's what matters.
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_06: Ozin taught me how to defend myself. Now I want to\nbe strong enough, so he doesn't have to worry!
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_07: It's better to learn how to use a blade than sit around\nin a classroom learning stuff. I'm right...right?
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_08: I love sweets. How about I bring you my favorites\nsometime?
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_09: There's a horrible guy who I know from my temple.\nI'm going to punch him if he treats me badly again.
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m02_10: I stole things before I worked for the temple. I'd get\npunished if caught and still have a scar. Wanna see?
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_01: Despite appearances, I carry more concerns than\nmost people. Could I rest at your side awhile?
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_02: I like lending a hand to those already trying to help\nthemselves. Does that make me a meddler?
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_03: Care to join me fishing? It's nice to spend time idly,\ncasting a fishing line.
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_04: The land of Dagda is full of interesting things. It'd be\nfascinating to explore it with you.
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_05: Do you detect anything...strange about how I look?\nI don't want to stand out.
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_06: People tell me I have a stern look much of the time.\nDo I really seem so harsh?
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_07: My daughter is currently in a long slumber. I hope to\nbe at her side by the time she awakens.
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_08: I enjoy writing fables. Are there any tales shared\namong birds? I'd love to hear them.
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_09: Your white appearance reminds me of someone very\nclose to me. I'd like a closer look.
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m02_10: I'm documenting all in this land to share with\nfuture generations. I'd like to look at you, please.
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_01: Yes, truly... It is wonderful fun, isn't it... What, can't\nyou see who I'm speaking with?
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_02: Death haunts me. Are you haunted by death?
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_03: I like being alone in my solitude. Do you too?
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_04: Looking at the clouds always is a balm for my hurt\nand heart. Would you join me, looking?
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_05: The spirits want to talk to you. They're...curious\nabout you.
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_06: I fear that my words enter the ear in strange ways.\nI am misunderstood...and avoided.
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_07: I would be grateful if you would pray with me, that\nwayward souls may move on to the next world.
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_08: When I look at someone, they in turn look away.\nIt seems that I am forever feared.
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_09: My mother died giving birth to me. My black garb\nserves as both mourning and atonement.
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m02_10: I have a strong dislike for insects. Could you chase\noff any who draw too close to me?
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_01: I would say I remain sharp despite my age. Wouldn't\nyou agree?
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_02: Is it obvious that I take painstaking care of\nmy beard?
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_03: Surely I do not lecture as much as they say. Do I?
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_04: One's duties must take precedence over all else.\nEven if the end result is divorce.
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_05: Do you believe a bright future awaits Saramis?
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_06: Future generations will surely surpass us. Hm!\nI look forward to it.
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_07: As they listened, the lovely maidens were enchanted\nby the bard's voice.
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_08: Of late, I find myself mired in dismal thoughts...
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_09: Looking at you gives me a sense of déjà vu. Why do\nyou suppose that is?
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m02_10: Would a wild and unfettered bird consider it cruel\nto be captured as a gift for my queen?
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_01: Love a good party! I wish we could have one\nevery day.
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_02: Gettin' old doesn't stop a guy from dominating on\nthe battlefield. You know what I'm saying?
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_03: Hey, is it a problem to go a few glasses past\nyour limit?
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_04: It's not a bad thing to drink until you fall asleep, is it?
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_05: I can still hold my own against anyone half my age!
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_06: Wine, mead, meat, and fish! That's what I call\na full meal!
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_07: I like to sing when I work. Puts me in a good mood.
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_08: *yawn* I'm in the mood for some shuteye.
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_09: It happened again! Some folks saw me and crossed\nthe street. Am I really that scary-lookin'?
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m02_10: You look like you wouldn't taste so good.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_01: Working for someone who doesn't trust you isn't\ntoo bad. The money's nice, at least.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_02: When I think about what I'll do with all this money\nI've saved...that's gonna be a great day.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_03: Would it be coldhearted of me to say that money's\nmore important to me than trust?
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_04: I like counting my savings over and over. Makes me\nfeel like I'm getting closer to my dream.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_05: Do you like sparkly things? Wanna see my gems?
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_06: Urgh... I wish the day would come that my whole\nfamily could live together like we used to.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_07: Your wings are so pretty. Let me get a better look.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_08: Next time I go hunting, I'll bring back some for you.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_09: When I've been working nonstop, sometimes\na breather does me a world of good.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m02_10: I'll have to be careful not to shoot you by mistake\nwhen I go hunting.
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_01: I like gazing at the sky. There's nothing silly about\nthat...right?
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_02: Despite the complaints, I have every right to refuse\na night's drinking. I don't tolerate alcohol well.
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_03: I'm considering if I should force myself to visit home.\nMy stepfather and I don't get along very well.
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_04: Am I too serious? Sometimes people react to me as if\nI was nagging them.
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_05: I must strive to surpass my father, so I can stand\nshoulder to shoulder with the brave veterans!
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_06: I bet it would feel incredible to fly alongside you in\nthe clouds.
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_07: I sometimes find my own inexperience frustrating...
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_08: Turning down the advances of passionate women\nwears on me, mentally and physically...
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_09: To look at you gives me the same feeling as when\nI gaze up at the sky.
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m02_10: Being with you puts me at such ease that I wish\nI could cage you to take you wherever I go.
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_01: Any scar you get in your lord's service is a badge\nof honor. Mine is handsome, don't you think?
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_02: When we were in hiding, I did all the cooking.\nWould you like me to make you something?
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_03: Most my age have had romantic relationships—I've\nonly had loyalty to my lord. But that's fine, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_04: When I lived in Cydonia, I tutored youths in combat.\nWould you like me to teach you some martial arts?
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_05: You're tenacious. If you were human, I'd want to\ntrain you as a knight.
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_06: Milady's heart is consumed with a desire for revenge.\nWhat I would do to free her from it...
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_07: The older I get, the more I find to grumble about.\nPerhaps I should work on that.
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_08: It's strange to see a bird with such conviction in\nits eyes.
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_09: I know well the sound of the vihuela. I'm sure it\nwould go beautifully with birdsong.
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m02_10: Let's say an enemy attacked while your charge stood\nbehind you. What would you do?
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_01: A bird's instrument is its chirp, but I'm no less skilled\nwith my own. Would you like to hear?
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_02: One must see the world in all its contours to melt\nothers' hearts as I do.
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_03: I am confident in my memory. No doubt I could\nrecognize you amidst a flock of winged creatures.
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_04: I'm envied by most men. Not that it's any wonder\nwhy. I mean, have you looked at me?
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_05: I detest shabby men. The sight of them sours my\nspirits. Is there something you similarly loathe?
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_06: The women of Kalla's temple are no longer seduced\nby my poetry. What else could I do to woo them?
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_07: Kalla is too resplendent for words. You ought to\nadmire for yourself what a marvel she is.
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_08: Considering my own skill in music, I thought we\nmight enjoy playing a song together. What say you?
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_09: The name given to me by my lady Kalla is so\nexcellent. Do you like your own name?
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m02_10: It was during a hailstorm that I was left at Kalla's\ntemple. So when you see hail, think of me.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_01: My mom loves singing, and she's AWFUL at it.\nYou seem like a good singer, though, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_02: I don't know where my dad is now. Hope he's eating\nand stuff.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_03: I'm pretty knowledgeable about medicinal herbs.\nIf you ever get injured, I'll fix you up!
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_04: I want to help people when they're in trouble. But I\ngotta get way stronger to do that!
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_05: Wanna try my cooking sometime? No one else will\neat it.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_06: I didn't think I had much in common with my mom,\nbut maybe she's where I got my pushiness.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_07: Sirocco's so great—I just really wish he didn't spend\nall his time womanizing.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_08: Everyone treats me like a kid. I wonder if that'll\never change.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_09: Back when Mom still lived at home, she'd train me!\nWanna give that a shot?
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m02_10: You have kind eyes. Looking at them really makes\nme feel better.
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_01: In either music or dance, one missed day of practice\ncosts you some skill. Never neglect your studies!
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_02: Oh dear, my handicraft turned out poorly again.\nI understand not why my artistic talent is failing me.
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_03: Listening to music played by another, I can\nsometimes feel their emotions. Do you share this?
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_04: I will best Leilidahna one day, I swear it. And I hope\nyou'll cheer me on!
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_05: Flowering trees bloom even as they get old. It proves\nthat age should not impede one's pursuits! Agreed?
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_06: Kalla is so lovely! I imagine you'd fall in love with\nher at first sight.
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_07: I was recognized as the Blue Rose of Caelus. Would\nyou like to hear me play?
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_08: I have the greatest confidence in my singing.\nAnd yourself?
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_09: Shall I compose a poem about you? If so, I'll do all I\ncan to make sure it pleases you...
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m02_10: What must motherhood be like? I can't help but find\nthe prospect terrifying.
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_01: I can't keep calm when someone picks a fight with\nme! Is it like that for birds too?
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_02: If you see someone in trouble, you should help them.\nIt's that simple!
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_03: Training's fun, but I get bored in a classroom. Who\nneeds books to be strong, anyway?
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_04: Martial arts tightens my mind and strengthens\nmy body! You should give it a try too!
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_05: Maybe I got a little too into my training?\nI'm sleepy now...
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_06: Everybody treats me like a kid just 'cause I'm short.\nIt's no good to judge folks on appearances, ya know?
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_07: Everybody's always yelling at me to be quiet. Am I\nreally that loud?
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_08: The people of the village were real nice to me, so I\nwanna try and make them happy.
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_09: You've got weird eyes. Ya know, they kinda remind\nme of Anatolia's.
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m02_10: We ate what we could get in the village. Even bugs.\nBack there, you woulda been a delicacy.
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_01: Our mission, the hopes of the villagers... It's all\nimportant, but so is protecting family, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_02: Your eyes are so charming. I wonder how mine look\nto you?
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_03: I have no idea what birds eat. Maybe you could let\nme try one of your meals sometime?
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_04: You're quite calm around humans. Aren't you afraid\nof creatures bigger than you?
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_05: I'm always drawn to people older than me. My first\nlove was like that. Is that why I can't forget them?
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_06: I'm always a little wary of talking to people from the\ntemples. What about you?
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_07: I love taking care of others. Do you think I could\npreen your feathers sometime?
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_08: It can be wonderful traveling the outside world.\nBut it does get scary sometimes.
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_09: If I'd remained in the village, I could be holding a\nbaby in my arms.
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m02_10: You've seen the world from up in the sky. I wish I\nspoke bird language. I bet you have a lot of stories.
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_01: My parents are gone, but I don't really feel lonely.\nI'm stronger than anyone, ya know!
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_02: Back in the village, we hunted and ate sandworms.\nI'll bring you some sometime!
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_03: I can tell how a building is put together with just\na glance. What about you?
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_04: I can tell you're interested in me. I'm a good-lookin'\nguy, so I can't blame ya!
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_05: Anatolia's always so hard on me. You think it's her\nway of flirting with me?
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_06: Being hungry can make ya sad. You ever need food,\nyou let me know.
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_07: Know what? I like you. How about if you join the\nDadao Gang? I'm strong, and I'll take care of you!
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_08: Everyone in the village is always hungry. I wanna\nmake it so they can all eat whenever they want.
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_09: Ya know, Anatolia was doing fortune-telling to earn\nmoney. I oughta teach you some tricks!
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m02_10: Nothing personal, but you don't really look that tasty.\nYou're all bones for one thing. I'll save you for last.
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_01: I think taste is more important than looks when it\ncomes to vegetables, don't you?
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_02: I'm good at crafts. I ought to try making something\nwith bird feathers, maybe.
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_03: I bought a cute accessory case the other day! But it\nwas cheap, and it broke the next day.
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_04: I can't fight as well as everybody else, but I can\nmaybe be useful in other ways, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_05: I saw a magician make a bird appear in their hand\nfrom nowhere! I want to try it. Can you shrink?
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_06: Nasshim used to take care of me. He was so nice.\nI still think about him sometimes...
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_07: It doesn't matter how long I'm gone, thinking of my\nfamily and my hometown makes me feel so lonely.
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_08: I like making sweets. Maybe I could make something\nsweet for you sometime.
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_09: When I think about the future, I always end up\nworrying about stuff I can't do anything about.
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m02_10: I've been thinking about my next performance, and I\nthink people would love it if we did a trick together!
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_01: I'm one of the most seasoned mercenaries here!\nDo I have the look of a battle survivor?
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_02: Are you living your life to the fullest? If not, why\nbother being alive at all!
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_03: My advice—make certain you're the one to make the\ncalls in battle. Otherwise, it's a sure way to die.
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_04: All this peace and quiet is making me sleepy. How\nabout you do something to wake me up?
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_05: I like your determined look. Hey, you know you can\ncount on the Unkillable Guzran, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_06: There are only so many meals we can eat in our\nlifetimes. Best to eat what you want, yeah?
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_07: The truth is—my true form is that of a bird. So I\nwonder, are you really a person?
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_08: Ha! A lady socked me real hard a little earlier.\nThat just means she was shy, yeah?
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_09: I earned my nickname, Unkillable Guzran, one scar\nat a time. Pretty cool, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m02_10: Lots of people got to where they are today because\nof me. One merc is now imperial inspector!
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_01: I have the odor of hitting the bottles too heavily.\nYet you don't mind. Do you enjoy a tipsy drink?
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_02: Practicing silence was part of my training. How\nabout you give it a try?
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_03: Some say that belief is the same as not thinking.\nI disagree. Not thinking is entirely different.
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_04: When my body has perished, and I float as a soul,\nlet's frolic in the sky. What do you say?
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_05: There is a saying that a bird flown from the coop is\ntruly still close to home. Does that sound right?
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_06: If birds have hearts, I wonder what kind beats under\nthose feathers of yours.
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_07: To live or die... To be tipsy or sober... These are\nsimilar states in a fleeting world. Don't you agree?
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_08: Birdsong makes everything better. It pairs especially\nwell with a fine drink. Wouldn't you say?
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_09: To think that I've put myself in the care of such a\ngroup of people. Fate is strange, isn't it?
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m02_10: I've heard of a monstrous bird who turned perfectly\ngood wine into poison. I trust that's not you?
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_01: Do you think we need someone to lead us? I believe\nin such an ideal, and I welcome your thoughts on it.
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_02: I'm not all that ill-tempered, really. I wonder if you'd\nlike to be more sociable too.
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_03: You bring a sort of calm atmosphere to a place.\nMind if I linger here a little longer?
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_04: I'm a bit tired. Forgive me if I fall asleep.
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_05: Do you think it wrong to accept payment from a\nlord you're drawn to serve?
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_06: My beloved steed, Rocinan, is aging very well.\nDo you think that when you see him?
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_07: I end up saying too much when talk turns to lords\nand their duties. Should I say less about it all?
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_08: It's natural to help one's friends and also the weak.\nBut it sometimes takes courage to do what's right.
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_09: What would you do if I said there's a venomous\nspider behind you? Let's practice. Drive it off...now!
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m02_10: Ha, you have an interesting face. I never get tired\nof seeing it.
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_01: You must visit our kingdom. We would feed and\nentertain you magnificently!
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_02: We are from Brigid, which is a kingdom that loves\nnature. So we enjoy our time with you.
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_03: We have enjoyed seafood since our earliest days and\nwould like to savor Dagdan specialties with you.
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_04: More of the people here grow to love us by the day.\nIs this the effect kings have on others?
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_05: We are very fond of the people of Brigid. So if you\nsee any, please tell us, alright?
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_06: You remind us of the spirits of our homeland.\nPerhaps we are connected somehow.
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_07: We deem you worthy of our protection, so if you're\never in trouble, please let us handle it!
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_08: We find ourselves bored at the moment. Can you\nperform any tricks?
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_09: We hope to take Lady Ultand as our queen, though\nsome consider her rank in society too low for us...
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m02_10: To learn the ways of a foreign land, there's no\nbetter way than to mingle with its people, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_01: I'd like to call you something more than "bird."\nHow's Birdlee? Nah, that's not right. Any advice?
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_02: I learned a lot living on a mountain, like hunting\nand blacksmithing. Good to have skills, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_03: I like fighting with my fists. Keeps me feeling free\nand nimble in battle. Get what I mean?
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_04: I grew up thinking you had to marry the person who\ncan defeat you in a fair fight. It's a dumb tradition,\nright? I'm tougher than the guys back home anyway.
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_05: I trained most days of my life, going up and down\nMount Orgus. Want me to kick your perch in half?
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_06: My third eldest brother is traveling the world like\nI am. Say hello if you see him. He loves animals.
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_07: Back home, I don't rank that high in importance, but\nas the chief's daughter, I'm singled out for marital\nchallenges. Can you see why I hate it back there?
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_08: Something good is coming up soon. My gut is always\nright, you know!
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_09: I want to add a new move to my wrestle-dancing.\nHave any great ideas?
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m02_10: You're always here alone. Did you leave your flock?\nI did something like that too. Let's be friends!
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_01: Mmm, roasted? Braised? Oh! Sorry, I didn't mean\nanything by it. You don't look tasty at all!
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_02: I never get tipsy, no matter how many mugs of suds\nI drink. How about you?
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_03: I like to give everyone cute little names. I hope it's\ncute anyway. Maybe it's kind of weird?
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_04: I was born and raised at Lyoshan Fort. If you ever\ngo there, watch out for all the ruffians!
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_05: I have a VERY healthy appetite. The pay I get from\nthe temple can't cover my meals. Tragic, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_06: Be careful not to get too near me when I'm really\nhungry. You do look delicious, I'm sorry to say.
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_07: I grew up enjoying food at my dad's feasts with his\nfriends. If I have a big party like that, want to come?
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_08: Don't you think Lord Solel is wonderful? He's so\nkind, amazing, and just plain great!
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_09: I love spicy food more than anything. Too bad it\nalways gets eaten up quick. Why is that, I wonder?
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m02_10: If I think someone's cute, I can't help calling them a\nfun name. I'm going to call you Li'l Birdie!
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_01: My pegasus has a refined palate and kicks away any\nfood that's not up to par. It's bad behavior.
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_02: I have a terrible scar that's hidden by my outfit.\nIt's proof that I fight bravely. Impressive, yes?
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_03: I've traveled for years, so I learned how to amuse\nmyself. Care to learn how to while away the time?
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_04: I keep hearing about people getting married...\nWhere is my ideal partner? I've been searching!
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_05: Always conduct yourself well, or it reflects badly on\nyour lord. Keep that in mind if you serve someone.
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_06: I can tell if a bird's singing voice is truly beautiful or\nnot. Is your song of sterling quality?
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_07: If you value top quality, you develop an eye for it.\nAnd I am a sterling knight, you know.
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_08: Caring for one's personal appearance is crucial.\nAre you taking good care of yourself?
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_09: My pockets are getting emptier, and so is my\nstomach. Maybe I'll just eat some bird food here...
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m02_10: I used to serve a noble. But a terrible incident led\nto his downfall. Very regrettable...
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_01: Don't worry. I have no interest in hunting you.\nI don't even like meat.
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_02: You have to learn a little bit about everything to\ngrow. What can I learn from your movements?
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_03: I studied hard to learn how to read and write. Do\nyou think you could do that too?
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_04: After I left my kingdom, I broke one of its laws by\nlearning to write. Yu Phas will surely punish me.
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_05: Lilian said she's happy just being around me. Can\nsuch a simple thing really make someone happy?
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_06: Mercenaries are more selective about work than\nyou'd think. People don't understand that.
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_07: I like eating sweet things. That surprises people.\nBut is that really so unexpected?
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_08: I've roved widely and welcome such long journeys.\nDo you migrate much?
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_09: I left my kingdom behind, but there are still many\nin Saramis who look up to me. I'm grateful.
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m02_10: People rely on me a lot, but I have to admit it'd be\nnice if I could rely on others more.
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_01: If anyone gets robbed or snuffed out...they shouldn't\nbe so weak! Fight harder, that's what I say!
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_02: Good idea not fighting anyone who looks too\ndangerous. Whoever lasts longest...wins, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_03: The mountains are like home to me. I should build\nme and my pals a castle up there, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_04: The guys in the Gaia Brigade left me for dead as\nsoon as we lost our battle in the games. Cruel, huh?
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_05: There's no way I can give up on pillaging now!\nYou know how many years I've been at it?
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_06: Got parents? If you don't, you'd fit in with me and\nmy pals just fine. You could join our bandit crew!
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_07: Weaklings like you end up as dinner. So try to fly\nextra-high so the arrows don't get you.
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_08: People think bandits eat nothin' but meat. It's\nvegetables all the way with me. Keep that in mind.
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_09: It's common sense to pick off the weaklings in\nbattle. You look like easy prey to me!
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m02_10: I thought I could get anything I want through plunder\nand fighting. But how can I get myself a family...
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_01: That damned Order of Mithras left me for dead.\nThey can't abandon the great Majide!
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_02: Nothin' better than smacking around nobodies when\nI'm annoyed. What do you do when you are?
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_03: Doesn't matter who comes at me—they're no match\nfor the great Majide, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_04: None of these grunts around here have a chance of\nbeating me. Why do they even try?
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_05: I shoved a mouthy drunk real hard. Felt pretty good,\nI gotta admit. But now it's time I catch some z's.
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_06: If my Southern Cross Brigade crew had battled in\nthe games, we would have won, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_07: Prison cells are my home away from home. Next\ntime I'm locked up, find me and we'll play a game!
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_08: Everyone knows the great Majide has the strength of\n10 men. How about I smash some rocks for you?
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_09: I'm bored as hell. Got a good move to show me?
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m02_10: You're not scared of me, which means you don't get\nhow great I am. How about I show you?
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_01: It's only a matter of time before you realize that I\nwas the best leader of this whole era!
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_02: Have you read the War Chronicle of Hasdrubal?\nI assure you, its scenes will thrill you to the core!
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_03: I despise a bland meal. I want a life of luxury.\nYou must want that too, yes?
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_04: I've got a secret under my eye patch that relates to\nmy past. I won't tell you about it though. HA!
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_05: No matter how many times you fail, your dream\ndoesn't die until you do. Good advice, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_06: Words like "repent," "regret," and "reform" are all\nstrange to me. But I suspect you do all of that.
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_07: I was a fine specimen of a man in my youth. No\nmatter where I went, people sang my praises!
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_08: Rarities fetch a high price, which is why I like them.\nNot that you'd know about such things.
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_09: It's harder to get a good night's sleep as I get older.\nI envy you juveniles and your deep sleep.
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m02_10: I am brilliant, amazing, dashing, and more! And I'm\na perfect general! You agree fully, correct?
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_01: Do you know the Order of Mithras? I'd suggest that\nyou steer clear of them.
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_02: I lose all track of time when I'm practicing with my\nbow. So if you see me at night, give a holler!
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_03: It's nice having family and friends to help when\nyou're in trouble. Always treasure your friends, OK?
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_04: Everyone back at my village speaks in a very unique\nway. Do birds have accents or dialects?
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_05: When I'm fighting, I'll say some horrifying things.\nLike I did when I possessed those awful remains.
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_06: I wonder how I would have fared in the Heroic\nGames if I didn't have Ugo's Bow...
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_07: I used to hunt birds with my bow. Ha! Want to see\nif you can outfly one of my arrows?
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_08: I'm not very skilled at dealing with men. Could you\nhelp me out if one harasses me?
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_09: "A brown cow with a crowned brow!" Ach, say that\nthree times fast, why don't ya?
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m02_10: I don't leave much of an impression on people.\nBut you're so beautiful I bet you do...
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_01: What's it like if you get hit by heavy rain while\nyou're flying?
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_02: I've traveled all over the land. Have you visited lots\nof places too?
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_03: When you love your family and it all falls apart,\nthat's about as bad as it gets, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_04: If someone settles down somewhere, a big home is\nbest to house a big family, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_05: I have things I want to protect. Is there something\nthat you want to protect?
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_06: When you do nothing but battle, you can end up\nfeeling pretty frazzled...
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_07: I don't value money over other things. But aren't\nthere things you can't protect without money?
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_08: You always seem to be alone. Don't you get lonely\nout there in the world, all by yourself?
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_09: Sometimes you've got to get sneaky if you want to\nsurvive. I mean, when you really have to!
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m02_10: I had a husband, you know. He died some time ago,\nbut I wonder if he watches over me.
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_01: I'm confident in my abilities in battle. I should show\nyou what I can do sometime!
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_02: Would you like to meet Bucephalus? It'd be fun if\nyou two were friends!
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_03: How do you take care of your feathers? They're\nso pretty.
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_04: I go on long rides every now and then. Would you\nlike to come along sometime?
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_05: It must be scary to live out in the wild. Please call for\nme if you're ever going somewhere dangerous!
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_06: It feels great to soar in the sky, doesn't it? How high\ncan you fly?
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_07: Have you ever been to my home in Tellus? It's a\nwealthy county and has an easiness to it. 
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_08: I'm trying to live up to the name of "Silver Maiden,"\nand with Bucephalus, I'm sure that I will!
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_09: I have nothing but happy memories of my parents.\nBut I do get sad, knowing they live only in memory.
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m02_10: I heard someone talking about me behind my back\nearlier. What should I do about that?
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_01: We must not isolate ourselves out of pride. That way\nis death. Do not forget this.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_02: City life is still strange to a forest-dweller like me.\nIf I get lost in Dagsion, would you show me the way?
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_03: We of the Har Hali live in harmony with nature.\nYou are not the first bird I would befriend.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_04: Birds have many meals each day, yes? I hope you eat\nwell and fly vigorously.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_05: My people use the behavior of animals as an omen\nfor battle. A bold attitude is a good omen.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_06: My skills did not live up to those of previous chiefs.\nHave I been of use to my people at all?
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_07: Rule based on strength only chokes the people. I'm\nsure you would also feel suffocated under oppression.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_08: I suspect no one could tarnish your wings. Keep true\nto your way of life. Let no one take you captive.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_09: Hm. These disheveled feathers must make it hard\nto fly. I'll straighten them for you.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m02_10: A mere graze from our poison arrows can fell a bird\ninstantly. Stay well away during our hunts.
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_01: You know a royal jerk who goes by Talimun? Peck\nout his eyes if you see him, alright?
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_02: What would you do if you saw a ghost? Truth be\ntold, I just faint dead away. Pathetic, I know...
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_03: That fool sank my ship, but I still see it sailing right\nand fine in my dreams. A beautiful vessel!
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_04: They say I'm successor to the legendary pirate\nDrake. His hideout was all mine. Incredible, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_05: My old crew used to love me. I hope they're doing\nalright. You think they'll join up with me again?
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_06: I've been praying a lot ever since I've been seeing\nghosts of those I killed. You pray too if you see 'em.
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_07: When I get my crew together, I swear I'll do no harm,\nonly look for treasure. Would you come with me?
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_08: I'm the Rukh, and you're a little bird. So you'll help\na friend out if I'm chased down, right?
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_09: The Order of Mithras is rotten to the core. They're\nfar more dangerous than pirates.
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m02_10: You should join my Black-Swan Pirates. I tell you,\nthere's nothing more fun than life as a pirate!
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_01: Nod.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_02: Nod timidly.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_03: Tilt your head.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_04: Turn away.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_05: Avert your eyes.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_06: Gaze intently.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_07: Look about.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_08: Look at the sky.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_09: Sing a beautiful tune.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_10: Sing softly.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_11: Sing with vigor.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_12: Sing boldly.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_13: Be intimidating.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_14: Preen.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_15: Spread your wings.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_16: Flap your wings.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_17: Flutter cheerfully.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_18: Dance.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_19: Get closer.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_20: Do a somersault.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_21: Tremble.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_22: Sit still.
MID_SV_Bird_Answer_23: Cling to your perch.
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m03_01: You're going? OK! Take care!
MID_SV_Bird_Kai1_m03_01: See you later. I'll be waiting!
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m03_01: You are departing, I see.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m03_01: Going, are you? Farewell, then.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m03_01: See you again.
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m03_01: Enjoy the skies.
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m03_01: Always a pleasure! Later, friend.
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m03_01: Take good care of your soul, alright?
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m03_01: We must part for a little while. Take care.
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m03_01: Goodbye. Please come back soon.
MID_SV_Bird_Tia1_m03_01: Goodbye. Take good care of yourself.
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m03_01: Alright. Let's meet again sometime?
MID_SV_Bird_Pet1_m03_01: Goodbye for now. Let's talk again soon!
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m03_01: I'd be very happy if I could see you again sometime!
MID_SV_Bird_Max_m03_01: Goodbye. Try not to get caught.
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m03_01: I'll let you go...this time.
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m03_01: Good thinkin'. Let's both go exercise!
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m03_01: Yes, fly freely, as a bird should.
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m03_01: Until next time, feathered one.
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m03_01: To live as a bird is to live without a care. A nice\nlife, hmm?
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m03_01: See you later! Take care not to get caught!
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m03_01: Make sure you eat a hearty meal when you get\nthe chance!
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m03_01: Right. I should get back to work as well.
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m03_01: Later, birdie.
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m03_01: I should be heading home. See you!
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m03_01: Thank you for spending time with me.
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m03_01: It's about that time. You go on, then...
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m03_01: Bye. You go right home, now!
MID_SV_Bird_Lor1_m03_01: See you. Don't get yourself hurt.
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m03_01: Hmm. Leaving already? Then I suppose I'll do\nthe same.
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m03_01: So it's time? I look forward to our next meeting.
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m03_01: Well then, take care.
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m03_01: See ya later.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m03_01: See you next time you're in the mood.
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m03_01: Are you flying off already?
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m03_01: Leaving already? Take care.
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m03_01: Ah yes, you must miss the skies. I'll go as well.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m03_01: Aw, going home? See you soon.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo1_m03_01: Going already? Let's talk again soon.
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m03_01: You soar wheresoever you wish! How lovely.
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m03_01: I'm headed home too. Take care.
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m03_01: You're going? Well then, I will too.
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m03_01: You leaving? See ya.
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m03_01: You're going home already? See you later!
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m03_01: What, you leaving? Guess that means it's about time\nto head to the tavern.
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m03_01: You depart, and so do I. May fate bring us\ntogether again!
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m03_01: You're going home? Then so will I. See you later.
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m03_01: Oh, leaving already? Then we, too, will depart.
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m03_01: It's about time that I do some training. So I have to\nsay goodbye for now.
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m03_01: I'm getting hungry, so I really should be going.
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m03_01: I am not accustomed to being left. That risks being a\ndire insult.
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m03_01: You're going? Well, take care of yourself.
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m03_01: Hopping to it already? Eager, aren't you?
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m03_01: Leaving so soon? Eh, you're no fun.
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m03_01: Where are you off to? You can't leave me!
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m03_01: Careful you don't hurt your wings.
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m03_01: You're going? Well, safe travels.
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m03_01: Be careful of the predators out there!
MID_SV_Bird_Cle_m03_01: 
MID_SV_Bird_Mys_m03_01: 
MID_SV_Bird_Nat_m03_01: I won't stop you. Take care.
MID_SV_Bird_Hri_m03_01: Taking off, then? You're a restless one.
MID_SV_Bird_Tro_m03_01: Going home? Take care of yourself.
MID_SV_Bird_Cen_m03_01: Such graceful wings. I hope you fly as far as you like.
MID_SV_Bird_Asw_m03_01: I will return to my duties as well.
MID_SV_Bird_Kou_m03_01: I suppose it was inevitable. Birds are meant to soar.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m03_01: Take flight, and never look back.
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m03_01: Leaving already? Must be nice, going off on a wind.
MID_SV_Bird_Kai0_m04_01: We'll meet again—I promise!
MID_SV_Bird_Kai1_m04_01: I look forward to seeing you again.
MID_SV_Bird_Dit_m04_01: I look forward to seeing you again.
MID_SV_Bird_Seo_m04_01: It seems you will not be tied down.
MID_SV_Bird_Led_m04_01: Stay out of trouble.
MID_SV_Bird_Bel_m04_01: Yes, fly free, and be safe.
MID_SV_Bird_Tal_m04_01: I wish I could stay, but I've got to get going.
MID_SV_Bird_Orh_m04_01: Always sad to part ways with you. Goodbye!
MID_SV_Bird_Anh_m04_01: Parting ways with someone I care about always\ncauses me to feel lonely.
MID_SV_Bird_Tia0_m04_01: Let's talk again, yeah? It's a deal!
MID_SV_Bird_Tia1_m04_01: We'll meet again. I promise I'll be waiting.
MID_SV_Bird_Pet0_m04_01: I'm going away now. It's going to be lonely, but I\nknow I'll see you again.
MID_SV_Bird_Pet1_m04_01: I'm going away now... Be well.
MID_SV_Bird_Hur_m04_01: Leaving already? I suppose you have your reasons.\nStill, I'll miss you.
MID_SV_Bird_Max_m04_01: Might as well enjoy the sky if you can.
MID_SV_Bird_Jes_m04_01: Yeah, enjoy your freedom...and take care.
MID_SV_Bird_Gol_m04_01: See ya! Don't get eaten!
MID_SV_Bird_Gat_m04_01: Stay strong until next time.
MID_SV_Bird_Dan_m04_01: Farewell, my avian friend! Enjoy the view!
MID_SV_Bird_Fab_m04_01: Do endeavor not to be caught by any beasts.
MID_SV_Bird_Esm_m04_01: See you around! Watch out for storms!
MID_SV_Bird_Mic_m04_01: It's sad to see you go, but free as a bird, as they say.
MID_SV_Bird_Urs_m04_01: Leaving already? Time flies, I suppose.
MID_SV_Bird_Sim_m04_01: See you later. Wish me luck!
MID_SV_Bird_Lou_m04_01: Let's talk again next time, alright?
MID_SV_Bird_Fia_m04_01: I hope we'll meet again...
MID_SV_Bird_Die_m04_01: Leaving? Watch out for other animals.
MID_SV_Bird_Lor0_m04_01: See you! Let's hang out again!
MID_SV_Bird_Lor1_m04_01: Come back sometime, OK? I'll be waiting!
MID_SV_Bird_Set_m04_01: Maybe you should rest your wings a little longer...
MID_SV_Bird_Nin_m04_01: Take care. I'll look forward to our next meeting.
MID_SV_Bird_Bon_m04_01: Going already? May we meet again.
MID_SV_Bird_Tob_m04_01: Leavin' already? Boo, you're no fun.
MID_SV_Bird_Lil_m04_01: I hope you come back. I'll be waiting.
MID_SV_Bird_Lys_m04_01: Can't say I blame you. The sky is a wonderful thing.
MID_SV_Bird_Buc_m04_01: I pray your feathers stay pure.
MID_SV_Bird_Sci_m04_01: I have little doubt that we shall meet again.\nTake care.
MID_SV_Bird_Moo0_m04_01: Looking forward to seeing you again! Buh-bye!
MID_SV_Bird_Moo1_m04_01: I wish we could've chatted longer. Take care.
MID_SV_Bird_Oly_m04_01: I shall miss you, but I would not tie you down...
MID_SV_Bird_Naz_m04_01: You're leaving already? Come back again, OK?
MID_SV_Bird_Sar_m04_01: You have to go? Take care of yourself.
MID_SV_Bird_Dai_m04_01: See ya later! Stay strong out there!
MID_SV_Bird_Hal_m04_01: I'd love to see you again, maybe. I'll be waiting!
MID_SV_Bird_Guj_m04_01: You take care. I'll have lived through some new epics\nby the time we next meet.
MID_SV_Bird_Yan_m04_01: Be well! Until next we meet!
MID_SV_Bird_Iio_m04_01: I enjoyed our time together. Let's do this again.
MID_SV_Bird_Pep_m04_01: Farewell! Until next time, live well and fly strong!
MID_SV_Bird_Noc_m04_01: See you later! Fly away from any critters that try to\nget near you!
MID_SV_Bird_Sop_m04_01: Be well, and don't be hungry!
MID_SV_Bird_Cat_m04_01: I won't keep you. I'm sure that we sterling friends\nwill meet again.
MID_SV_Bird_Ned_m04_01: I look forward to our next meeting. Goodbye.
MID_SV_Bird_Zac_m04_01: Stick around longer next time, OK? I'll be around!
MID_SV_Bird_Maj_m04_01: Fun stuff! I look forward to talking again.
MID_SV_Bird_Ven_m04_01: Going already? I've got more to feed you!
MID_SV_Bird_Ini_m04_01: Ach! Stay alive and come back, OK?
MID_SV_Bird_Jas_m04_01: Thank you for the visit. I look forward to seeing\nyou again.
MID_SV_Bird_Ale_m04_01: Why do nice times never last...
MID_SV_Bird_Cle_m04_01: 
MID_SV_Bird_Mys_m04_01: 
MID_SV_Bird_Nat_m04_01: Stay safe and come back. I'll wait for you.
MID_SV_Bird_Hri_m04_01: I don't wish to part, but I won't stop you. Take care.
MID_SV_Bird_Tro_m04_01: You're a restless one. But I think I'll be seeing you\nagain sometime.
MID_SV_Bird_Cen_m04_01: There's no need to hurry. But be well in your travels.
MID_SV_Bird_Asw_m04_01: Take care! Let's rest our wings together soon.
MID_SV_Bird_Kou_m04_01: Visit again. There's a weight in me that lifts when\nI'm with you.
MID_SV_Bird_Nuz_m04_01: Until we meet again, I will remember the sight of\nyour graceful wings.
MID_SV_Bird_Kir_m04_01: Until the winds bring us together again, little friend!